  "historical_rows_closed": {
    "602": "Compared the full historical projectile implementation. The projectile owns the original floor query and uses a const start vector and typed shooter. Movement, the five-frame floor refresh, lifetime, wall test and target height test retain the original code and data. The current owner lookup and attack payload cover the original semantics with their existing names",
    "713": "Reviewed the complete historical base declaration against the native 0x430 Epsilon class and constructor in text_803626A8.cpp. The four fades follow the common enemy state. The historical copy_position and update_angle additions have no linked definitions, so the current interface omits the unused declarations"
  },
